mpf (3.8.3~20260713172204.8602d4dd-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Point MPF at the PINNED redumper732 instead of the rolling redumper, in both
    the metadata (Recommends) and the config the wrapper seeds. b732 is the build
    MPF's publish-nix.sh bundles, so an MPF dump now runs the dumper build its
    upstream actually tested with.
  * The pin exists even though the rolling redumper package carries the very same
    build today. That equality is an accident of timing: the rolling package moves,
    and the day b733 lands, an MPF pointed at it would silently dump with a build
    it was never tested against -- MPF has no version check of any kind and would
    never say so.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Tue, 14 Jul 2026 03:45:00 +0000

