mpf (3.8.3~20260713042509.813e8305-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Ship the launcher icon in all standard hicolor sizes. We had 32/64/128/256/512
    as five pre-rendered PNGs in debian/; the sizes a panel or dock actually asks
    for -- 16, 22, 24, 48 -- were missing, so the desktop downscaled the 32 (or the
    512) on the fly for every taskbar slot.
  * Now ONE master (debian/mpf-512.png) is kept and the rest is rendered at build
    time with a Lanczos filter. Five files that must stay in lockstep are five
    chances to update four of them. The dropped PNGs were plain downscales anyway
    -- measured (RMSE < 0.02 against a fresh resample) before removing them.
  * New Build-Depends: imagemagick. The CLI name differs by series (IM6 has only
    `convert`, IM7 only `magick`), so debian/rules resolves it in the build root
    instead of hardcoding either. Both paths were built: bookworm (IM6) and
    trixie (IM7).
  * debian/rules fails the build if any icon size is missing or empty.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:40:00 +0000

